            DIGITAL ANNOUNCES WORLD'S FASTEST WORKSTATION


MAYNARD, Mass. -- April 3, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today unveiled its AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation -- the world's 
fastest workstation. Priced at $19,995 for a fully configured 
system, the new workstation is designed to meet the demanding needs 
of scientists and engineers in technical markets such as Mechanical 
CAD, Electrical CAD, Geographic Information Systems, and science and 
research. It runs three operating systems -- Digital UNIX, OpenVMS, 
and Microsoft's Windows NT Workstation.

     This high-performance desktop workstation has a clock rating of 
266 MHz, and SPECint92 and SPECfp92 of 198.6 and 262.5 respectively. 
It offers customers better performance and price/performance than 
workstations from competitors, including all of Hewlett-Packard's HP 
715 and 735 workstations, IBM's 3CT and 59H workstations, Sun's 
SPARCstation workstations, and Silicon Graphic's Indigo2 and 
PowerIndigo2 workstations. 

     "With the AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation, our customers get 
an unbeatable combination -- a powerful system and the world's 
fastest 2D graphics performance available at any price," said 
Philippe Ribeyre, vice president of Digital's Workstation Business 
Segment. "In addition, our customers in technical markets can run 
the top applications from the industry's leading Independent Software 
Vendors (ISVs) such as Parametric Technology Corporation, Matra 
Datavision, ComputerVision, Mentor Graphics, Synopsis, Viewlogic, 
ESRI, and Genetics Computer Group, to name a few." 

     Parametric Technology Corporation of Waltham, Mass., is the 
leading supplier of mechanical design software used by more than 
5,000 companies throughout the world.  The company is one of a 
number of ISVs expecting Digital's new workstation to be a big 
seller. "At PTC, we recognize that every day saved in the 
design-through-manufacturing cycle positively affects our customer's 
bottom line," said Olimpio DeMarco, manager of strategic relations 
for Parametric Technology Corporation. "Certifying the Pro/ENGINEER 
family of mechanical CAD/CAM software on a high-performance 
workstation like the AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation enables 
Pro/ENGINEER customers to take advantage of excellent hardware 
price/performance to further reduce their time to market." 

     Environmental Systems Research Institute, Inc. (ESRI), based in 
Redlands, Cal., is the market leader and pioneer in Geographic 
Information Systems (GIS) solutions. ESRI is another ISV that 
envisions many sales of the new workstation. 

     "The AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation sets a new performance 
standard for Digital's workstation product line," said Tom Murdoch, 
manager of hardware vendor alliances at ESRI. "Mapping applications 
utilize a large amount of disk storage and challenge the graphics 
capabilities of a workstation. The AlphaStation 250 4/266 
workstation more than meets the needs of our users because of its 
outstanding 2D graphics performance, storage capacity, and overall 
performance." 

     The AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation is another 
channels-ready product from Digital. It was designed and packaged 
with industry standard components such as the PCI bus, which enables 
a wide range of peripherals to be available from third-parties. The 
new workstation is available and shipping worldwide through 
Digital's premier network of channel partners, ISVs, and directly 
through Digital's Account Business Unit. 

     The AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation comes with a three-year 
hardware warranty, featuring next-day response and onsite service 
for the first year. Digital is the only vendor in the industry to 
offer a three-year hardware warranty for workstations. 

     An AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation with the Digital UNIX or 
OpenVMS operating system, 32 MBytes of memory, a 1.44 MByte floppy 
disk, a 1.05 GByte hard disk, a 600 MByte CD-ROM, ZLXp-E1 8-plane 
2D/3D graphics, and a 21-inch color monitor is $19,995. 

     An AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation with the Windows NT 
Workstation operating system, 32 MBytes of memory, a 1.44 floppy 
disk, 535 MByte hard disk, 600 MByte CD-ROM, DEC864 2D graphics, and 
a 17-inch color monitor is $13,890.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
