                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
 
                             FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:  AlphaStation 250 4/266 Workstation


OVERVIEW:

The newest member of the AlphaStation family, the AlphaStation 250 
4/266 workstation, is the world's fastest workstation. It was 
especially designed for engineers or scientists who requires a 
high-performance system to run demanding graphics applications.

The AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation has a clock rating of 266 
MHz, and SPECint92 and SPECfp92 performance of 198.6 and 262.5 
respectively. It offers customers better performance and 
price/performance than workstations from competitors, including 
Hewlett-Packard's HP 715 and 735 workstations, IBM's 3CT and 59H 
workstations, SGI's Indigo2 and PowerIndigo2 workstations, and all 
of Sun's uniprocessor SPARCstation workstations. 

The AlphaStation 250 4/266, housed in a low-profile desktop 
enclosure, accepts both PCI and ISA options available from Digital 
and its business partners. The workstation is highly expandable with 
memory capacity of up to 256 MBytes (512 MBytes in the future) and 
internal storage of over 3 GBytes and 13.6 GBytes total storage, 
including external storage. It contains an embedded Fast SCSI-2 
controller for disks and tapes and an Ethernet controller for 
networking. It is multimedia equipped with built-in CD-quality audio 
in/out and multimedia software. A range of PCI-based video options 
are available. 

New features such as the 128-bit wide memory bus and on-board cache 
of 2 MBytes make technical applications run faster on the 
AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation than on any other workstation. It 
is the fastest 2D graphics workstation in the world available at any 
price. 

The workstation supports three operating systems -- Digital UNIX, 
OpenVMS, and Windows NT Workstation. 

The system runs the top applications for Mechanical Computer-Aided 
Design (MCAD), Mechanical Computer-Aided Engineering (MCAE), 
Electrical Computer-Aided Design (ECAD), and Geographic Information 
Systems (GIS). Applications from leading Independent Software 
Vendors (ISVs) are available, including software from Parametric 
Technology Corporation, Matra Datavision, ComputerVison, Mentor 
Graphics, Synopsis, Viewlogic, ESRI, Smallworld, and many others. 
The workstation will be widely used for science and research 
applications. 

The AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation was especially designed for 
sale through indirect channel partners. It is based upon industry 
standard enclosures, options, and SIMM memory so resellers can 
streamline their inventories. The workstation also comes with the 
best warranty for workstations in the industry. Digital includes a 
three-year warranty with one year of on-site service and 90 days of 
software telephone support. 


