            NEW MULTIMEDIA PRODUCTS ENHANCE ALPHASTATION
                      WORKSTATIONS APPLICATIONS


       Digital Announces Support for Intel's Indeo File Format
                  and New Video Capture/Output Card


MAYNARD, Mass., April 3, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today
further enhanced the multimedia capabilities of its AlphaStation
workstations with new features for Multimedia Services for Digital 
UNIX software, and a new video capture and output card--FullVideo 
Supreme. 

     Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX is the multimedia 
programming interface and set of productivity tools for AlphaStation 
workstations. New features provide users and developers with access 
to more industry standard video file formats, including MPEG-1, 
widely used across the Internet, and Intel's Indeo, which enables 
the sharing of audio and video data with PCs. FullVideo Supreme 
allows users to develop and run multimedia applications that 
incorporate full-motion video, video clips, and stills when used in 
conjunction with Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX. 

     Multimedia, the combination of audio, video, text, graphics, 
and animation, is used in applications such as collaborative 
computing, desktop conferencing, training, presentations, video 
editing, and others for engineering, business, education, and 
entertainment. Digital's AlphaStation workstations are an excellent 
choice for multimedia applications because of their fast processing 
speeds, built-in multimedia capabilities such as high-fidelity audio, 
microphones, and headphones, and open PCI architecture, enabling the 
availability of a wide range of third-party options. 

     "Multimedia is changing the way people work and is a powerful 
method for presenting and manipulating information," said Philippe 
Ribeyre, vice president of Digital's Workstation Business Segment. 
"Digital's AlphaStation workstations, with their fast CPUs and 
tightly integrated audio and video subsystems, are the best 
workstations on the market to take advantage of this breakthrough 
technology. Today's announcements further strengthen Digital's 
multimedia workstation offerings. For example, Digital is the first 
workstation vendor to offer compatibility with Intel's Indeo video 
file format.  And the new FullVideo Supreme video card for the 
capture, editing, and display of video images, delivers many of the 
features found only on higher-priced video cards." 

     These new capabililities are important for multimedia 
applications from Independent Software Vendors (ISVs) such as 
Insoft, Inc., the world's leader in LAN/WAN-attached desktop 
conferencing solutions, and a key technology and marketing partner 
for Digital. The company's Communique! software for collaborative 
computing and desktop conferencing is the only application to 
provide conferencing across Windows, Windows NT, and UNIX-based 
platforms. 

     "The AlphaStation product line already has a strong presence in 
key vertical market segments such as financial services, Mechanical 
Computer-Aided Design, and Geographic Information Systems," said 
Daniel L. Harple, Jr., Chairman & CEO, Insoft, Inc.  "The 
combination of the superior price/performance and large storage 
capacities of AlphaStation products with Multimedia Services for 
Digital UNIX software will help Digital achieve broader deployment 
of workstations for collaborative computing and desktop conferencing 
in these markets." 

     Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX software is included free 
of charge with every AlphaStation workstation running the Digital 
UNIX operating system. A developers license is available for $395. 
FullVideo Supreme is priced at $895. Both products are available and 
shipping. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
