                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
 
                             FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:  Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX


OVERVIEW:

Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX is the multimedia programming 
interface for Digital's AlphaStation workstations running the 
Digital UNIX operating system. It also provides multimedia 
productivity tools for users to access audio and video subsystems 
that are available on Digital's AlphaStation workstations. 

Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX allows application developers 
and end users alike to take advantage of capture, playback, and 
manipulation of multimedia with their applications. Multimedia data 
can also be integrated with productivity applications to deliver the 
benefits of multimedia to common, everyday applications. 

Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX is based on Microsoft's Video 
for Windows interface, the multimedia Applications Programming 
Interface (API) that enables PC application developers to add sound 
and video to new or existing applications.  The use of an 
industry-standard interface enables AlphaStation workstation users 
to share audio and video data with PCs. It also allows developers 
with PC experience to get started immediately, without expensive and 
time-consuming training. The developer's license is available for 
only $395.

Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX incorporates a set of runtime 
libraries and productivity tools and user interfaces that lets any 
AlphaStation workstation user take advantage of desktop multimedia 
capabilities. This runtime software is included free of charge on 
all AlphaStation workstations running the Digital UNIX operating 
system. Software video playback and software compression are 
included with the package. This means users can play back digitized, 
stored video in software full motion, utilizing industry-standard 
JPEG, MPEG-1, or Intel's Indeo file formats. Users can also compress 
standard software video files in JPEG and Indeo formats. 

The CPU performance of Digital's Alpha chip coupled with Digital's 
AccuVideo rendering technology makes software video playback run 
faster and look better on Digital's AlphaStation workstations. 
Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX offers both application 
developers and end users a unique opportunity to tap the full 
potential of multimedia computing. 

