          DIGITAL'S STORAGE BUSINESS UNIT UNVEILS WIDE SCSI
               STRATEGY FOR STORAGEWORKS PRODUCT LINE


       New Storage Solutions Provide Customers with Additional
                        Interconnect Choices


MAYNARD, Mass. -- April 3, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced a core strategy for the introduction of wide SCSI 
storage technology to its StorageWorks product line.  The company is 
rolling out new wide SCSI storage products over the next 12 to 18 
months as an increasing number of wide SCSI components become 
available to provide clear performance advantages to its customers.  
As part of this strategy, Digital today introduced a range of new 
wide SCSI offerings targeting specific applications, becoming the 
first provider of wide SCSI products for Digital computing 
platforms.

     Digital has based its product roll-out strategy on the fact 
that wide SCSI direct-connect solutions offer significant 
performance benefits in select high-bandwidth applications.  By 
directly attaching wide SCSI products to computing systems with high 
performance busses, such as PCI, users can achieve gains in 
performance and throughput efficiency when running applications with 
large numbers of large data transfers.  Such applications include 
host-based RAID 0, seismic, telemetry and imaging.

     "In some instances, wide SCSI solutions can provide tremendous 
performance gains, particularly when host-based RAID 0 is 
utilized,"said Robert Passmore, manager of strategy and technology 
for Digital's Storage Business Unit.  "Digital is committed to 
evaluating wide SCSI technologies as they become available and 
incorporating them in storage products where they provide our 
customers higher performance and cost savings.  Our ultimate goal 
is to offer maximum choice -- of storage media, interconnect 
technologies, and configuration options, while aggressively lowering 
total storage cost of ownership."

     Today's announcement follows closely the Storage Business 
Unit's March 7, 1995 introduction of new PCI storage solutions.  
According to Edward McCarren, Digital UNIX(R) marketing manager 
for Digital's Storage Business Unit, these recent StorageWorks PCI 
product introductions offer significant storage system performance 
and data availability gains for the large and growing base of 
Digital's AlphaServer customers.  

     "Our PCI announcement demonstrated our strengths in leveraging 
emerging technologies that deliver significantly faster throughput 
and higher availability.  Today's announcement extends that 
capability with wide SCSI storage subsystems that directly attach to 
the PCI bus, allowing customers to take full advantage of available 
bandwidth for even greater productivity gains," McCarren said.

New StorageWorks Wide SCSI Solutions

     Digital today introduced three StorageWorks wide SCSI products 
for Alphaserver 2100 systems running the Digital UNIX operating 
system.  This announcement complements Digital's recently-available 
wide SCSI offerings for HP-UX, Sun, IBM AIX, and Novell NetWare 
platforms.  

The offerings introduced today include:

Wide SCSI Disk Drives -- RZ26L-W and RZ28-W

     Based on fast-wide 16-bit SCSI technology, the StorageWorks 
RZ26L-W (1 GB) and RZ28-W (2 GB) disk drives for Digital UNIX 
customers offer high bandwidth SCSI support of 20 MB per second.  
Both 3.5-inch devices provide data access times of 15.1 MS, average 
seek times of 9.5 MS, and are backwards compatible to ensure 
investment protection.  Priced at $950 for the RZ26L-W and $1829 for 
the RZ28-W, both disk drives come with a 5-year warranty, including 
a 1-year on-site warranty.

DWZZB 16-Bit SCSI Bus Extender/Signal Converter

     The new StorageWorks DWZZB-VW single-ended to differential SCSI 
bus converter handles data rates up to 20 MB per second on fast 
SCSI, while allowing maximum extension of the SCSI bus with no 
performance degradation.  Designed for more powerful 16-bit SCSI 
buses, the DWZZB extends the SCSI bus from 3/6 meters to 25 meters, 
and is fully compatible with the 2-5 MB per second data rates of 
earlier SCSI interconnects.  Priced at $600, the DWZZB-VW offers a 
1-year on-site and an additional 2-year return-to-factory warranty.

BA356-KC Wide Deskside Expansion Unit

     The StorageWorks BA356-KC Wide Deskside Expansion Unit supports 
the newly-introduced 16-bit RZ26L-W (1 GB) and RZ28-W (2 GB) disks, 
and the DWZZB-VW 16-bit single-ended to differential SCSI bus 
converter. In addition, the BA356-KC supports the recently-announced 
KZPSA high-performance wide SCSI to PCI adapter and the high-
performance StorageWorks 7200 RPM disk drives. The BA356-KC is priced 
at $1,200 and includes a shelf, power supply, pedestal kit and power 
cord.  Digital offers an accompanying 1-year on-site and an additional 
2-year return-to-factory warranty.

     StorageWorks products for Digital platforms and operating 
environments are available through authorized distributors, from the 
Digital sales force, and through DECdirect and the ESTORE.  For more 
information about Digital's complete line of StorageWorks products, 
call 1-800-STORWORK.

     The StorageWorks product line is a comprehensive family of 
disk, tape, and optical storage subsystems, offering modular, 
competitively-priced, industry-standard solutions in customizable 
desktop, Deskside, departmental, and datacenter enclosures.  
StorageWorks products are available on multiple operating systems 
and hardware platforms, including Digital workstations, systems and 
servers, Novell and Windows NT environments, and Hewlett-Packard, 
IBM, and Sun workstations and servers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
