                             FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:  FullVideo Supreme Video Card


OVERVIEW:

Digital's FullVideo Supreme is a video capture and output card. When 
used in conjunction with Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX, users 
can develop and use multimedia applications that incorporate both 
full motion video, video clips, and stills.  Users can also develop 
cross-platform video and multimedia applications, bridging the gap 
between Alpha and Intel hardware platforms. 

The FullVideo Supreme video card delivers many of the features found 
in higher-priced cards, enabling users to perform world-class video 
rendering with dithering and control of brightness, contrast, 
saturation, and image sharpness without having to pay for features 
that they may not need. 

The FullVideo Supreme video card can operate on any graphics 
subsystem, which means that commodity as well as high-end 3D 
graphics options can be used with it. Its analog video input allows 
for the use of cameras, VCRs, and laser disks. Through its video 
output capabilities, users can record to a VCR tape or play video 
back on a TV monitor. The video card provides superb image quality 
for a given number of colors, dynamically maps video to window size, 
and supports multiple video file formats and standard connectors. 

Multimedia--a combination of audio, video, text, graphics, and 
animation--is a powerful method for presenting and manipulating 
information. Digital's FullVideo Supreme video card helps users add 
a critical component by allowing them to capture incoming video and 
incorporate it into a wide range of applications for engineering, 
business, education, and entertainment. 

HIGHLIGHTS:

    o  Supported on any Alpha PCI-bus workstation independent of 
       graphics subsystem for capture and display

    o  Real-time NTSC full-frame or NTSC, PAL, or SECAM full-field 
       capture of video images

    o  Analog output to store on a video tape or to display on a TV 
       monitor

    o  Performs hardware filtering to improve compression and 
       quality of video

    o  AccuVideo rendering provides high-quality images with fewer 
       colors
 
SPECIFICATIONS: 

Video input standards						    
    
    NTSC,  640x480, 30 frames/sec
                    60 fields/sec
    PAL,   768x576, 50 fields/sec
    SECAM, 768x576, 50 fields/sec

Video output standards						    
    
    NTSC,  640x480, 30 frames/sec
    PAL,   768x576, 50 fields/sec

Pixel encodings							    
    								    
    YUV 4:2:2 interleaved
    8-bit pseudo-color
    24-bit color (conversion through software)
    
Video Connections						    

    RCA composite video input
    RCA composite video output


PRICING AND AVAILABILITY:

The FullVideo Supreme video card is $895 and is available and 
shipping.							    
