              DIGITAL INTRODUCES CONFIGURATION SWITCHES
                     TO BUILD VIRTUAL LANS TODAY


           ...Now Delivering the Most Feature-Rich Family
           of High-Performance Switches in the Industry...


LAS VEGAS, Nevada, March 27, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today expanded its leadership in switched networking by introducing 
two new port-level configuration switches, enabling network managers 
to meet the increasing network performance demands of their users 
and applications.  Combined with its flexible DEChub 900 MultiSwitch 
architecture, full family of high-performance LAN switches and 
powerful management software, Digital enables network managers to
provide virtual LAN capabilities today.

     With the new products -- the Portswitch 900 family and the 
latest version of HUBwatch management software -- the network 
manager can effectively address the major issues facing high-
performance networks today:  optimizing existing bandwidth to 
support today's powerful client/server and desktop applications; 
reducing costly and time-intensive adds, moves, and changes; and 
ensuring a secure networking environment for workgroups and project 
teams -- all with industry-leading product features and pricing.

     "Digital is now providing customers with the best of both 
worlds -- configuration and LAN switching integrated in a flexible 
backplane architecture," said Nick Lippis, president of Strategic 
Networks Consulting, Inc. "The DEChub family, coupled with the 
GIGAswitch products enable Digital to provide switching capabilities 
where customers require them." 

PORTswitch 900 Family of Per-Port Switching Products

     The PORTswitch 900 family of products are high-density, 
Ethernet configuration switches that can logically interconnect any 
combination of ports to individual, secure, LAN segments.  As with 
all DEChub products, the PORTswitch 900 configuration switches offer 
the unique capability to be implemented as either as a standalone
DEChub ONE stackable solution or as a module in the modular DEChub 
900 MultiSwitch.

Products announced today include:

     o	The PORTswitch 900TP, a 32-port, 10-BaseT configuration 
        switch
     o	The PORTswitch 900CP, a 16-port, 10-Base2 (Thinwire) 
        configuration switch

     The two new PORTswitch products now bring configuration 
switching from the backbone, with the fiber optic PORTswitch 900FP, 
to the desktop.  Each product includes port-level security features 
to prevent unauthorized eavesdropping or broadcasting.  In addition, 
the PORTswitch 900TP and PORTswitch 900FP configuration switches 
support redundant link configurations for improved reliablity.  

     The PORTswitch 900TP and PORTswitch 900CP configuration 
switches are priced at $5,500 and will be available in May 1995.  
The PORTswitch 900FP is priced at $5,990 and is available 
immediately.

     HUBwatch Version 4.0 -- Low-cost Virtual LAN Management from a 
PC Also new today is the latest version of HUBwatch, Digital's 
graphical SNMP network managment software.  HUBwatch manages the 
full family of DEChub products, including the new PORTswitch family.  
HUBwatch Version 4.0 for Windows also adds support for the 
GIGAswitch/ATM, Digital's industry-leading ATM switch for high-
performance networks.  Digital provides customers with the broadest 
range of switching solutions, all manageable from a single 
management platform. Digital is also the only vendor delivering the 
capability to create and manage virtual LANs from a low-cost, 
easy-to-use PC platform.  

     In addition to native support on Windows, UNIX, OpenVMS systems 
and enterprise management platforms such as HP OpenView, POLYCENTER 
Netview, and Digital's ManageWorks, HUBwatch Version 4.0 adds 
support for Novell NMS management environments.  Combined with the 
Novell-certified DEChub products, Digital provides a powerful, 
reliable basis for building Novell networks.

     Full HUBwatch functionality is available now on PC platforms 
for $495.  HUBwatch Version 4.0 will be available in May 1995 for 
the same price.  Current HUBwatch customers can upgrade to Version 
4.0 for as little as $99. 

     "At Children's Hospital, the staff's needs are always changing 
-- plus we have a 20 percent annual growth rate -- so it's important 
to be able to make network adds, moves, and changes quickly and 
easily," said Jim Hutchinson, network analyst at Children's Hospital 
in Boston.  "Digital's switching products give me a lot of 
flexibility and performance.  The new PORTswitches will enable me to 
configure LAN segments from a PC and group individual users, which 
is the first phase of our implementation of virtual LANs." 

Digital Knows Networks

     "Digital has the strategy and products to deliver virtual LAN 
capabilities to customers today, and offers the most comprehensive, 
robust set of high-performance LAN switches in the industry," said 
William Maro, vice president of product marketing and engineering 
for Digital's Network Product Business.  "Today's announcement 
provides key components for enVISN, Digital's comprehensive 
networking strategy, architecture, and product roadmap."

     Building on a strong tradition of technological excellence, 
Digital is leading the way in the networking industry today.  
According to revenue figures from the International Data Corporation 
(IDC), Dataquest, and Rising Star Research, Digital holds the number 
three market position in routers, hubs and LAN switching markets, 
and holds the number two position in FDDI products.  Digital's 
Network Product Business has pioneered a new, converged model for 
networking in which hubs, routers and switches are deployed on an 
integrated platform.  In addition, Digital's expertise in network 
integration services has connected more than 12 million users 
worldwide.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software, and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
