                 APPLE, ASANTE, AND MOTOROLA CHOOSE
          DIGITAL'S PCI ETHERNET CHIPS FOR NETWORK CONTROL


 ...Industry Leaders Select Digital Semiconductor Networking Chips...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 28, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that Apple Computer, Asante Technologies, and 
Motorola Computer Group have expressed their intent to build 
computer products incorporating PCI Ethernet controller chips from 
Digital Semiconductor, a Digital Equipment Corporation business.

     Apple Computer, Cupertino, California, has selected Digital 
Semiconductor's PCI-based 21040 10Mbps (megabits per second) and 
21140 10/100Mbps Ethernet controllers to develop network interface 
cards for the Macintosh and PC Windows environments.  "Digital 
Semiconductor's excellent upward migration path and the outstanding 
price/performance of its Ethernet and Fast Ethernet chips make it 
the logical choice for us," said Bill Brown, Business Unit Manager, 
ABS (Apple Business Systems) Connectivity Products.

     Asanti Technologies' Bruce Stancombe said that the San 
Jose-based company will incorporate the 21140 Fast Ethernet chip in 
its AsantiFAST PCI Fast Ethernet implementation.  Stancombe, 
Director of Product Marketing, said, "We chose Digital 
Semiconductor's Fast Ethernet chip because of the low CPU 
utilization and full-duplex capabilities.  The Fast Ethernet chip, 
combined with Asanti's proven Ethernet card design, delivers a 
high-performance solution to the customer." 

     Jerry Gipper is Director of Marketing, Embedded Technologies, 
in the Motorola Computer Group, which is using the 21040 PCI 
Ethernet controller in several motherboards and on a VME board.  
"The 21040 Ethernet controller is very easy to integrate and has met 
all our performance expectations," he said.  "But perhaps its most 
attractive feature is its clear, straightforward upgrade path to the 
21140 Fast Ethernet controller.  For us, that was a real plus."  

     Digital Semiconductor's 21140 PCI Fast Ethernet LAN controller 
is a high-performance device with both 100Mbps and 10Mbps ports, 
providing users the easiest and fastest route from 10BaseT to 
100BaseT Ethernet in PCI-based, mixed-platform, mixed-operating 
system environments.  Both the 21140 PCI Fast Ethernet and 21040 PCI 
Ethernet controllers act as PCI bus masters, featuring a direct 
memory access (DMA) architecture to optimize CPU utilization, and 
support full-duplex operation.  Both chips are supported with 
software drivers for all major operating system environments.  

     William N. Johnson, Vice President, Digital Semiconductor 
Marketing and Sales, commented, "We are very pleased that these 
well-known industry leaders have selected our networking chips for 
their products.  Their choice of our PCI Ethernet controllers 
clearly demonstrates the performance and product leadership of our 
networking chips in a very competitive market." 

     Digital Semiconductor, a Digital Equipment Corporation business 
headquartered in Hudson, Massachusetts, designs, manufactures and 
markets industry-leading semiconductor products including Alpha 
microprocessors and PCI-based peripheral chips.  It has also 
announced that it will design, manufacture, and market StrongARM 
low-power, high-performance 32-bit RISC microprocessors.  
PCI products include networking chips, bridge chips, and graphics/
multimedia accelerators that offer industry-leading performance and 
functionality for all major platforms, both CISC and RISC.  Digital 
Semiconductor operates design centers in Hudson;  Palo Alto, 
California;  Austin, Texas;  and Jerusalem, Israel.  Semiconductor 
products are manufactured in Hudson and South Queensferry, Scotland.  
Digital Semiconductor sells its products worldwide through its 
direct sales force and semiconductor distribution channels. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
