               DIGITAL AND DIGITAL RENAISSANCE INC. TO
                CO-DEVELOP KEY TOOLS AND APPLICATIONS
                      FOR INTERACTIVE SERVICES


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 28, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Digital Renaissance Inc., of Toronto, today announced a joint 
relationship for co-developing interactive applications and 
production tools for Digital's media server platform. 

     Interactive applications, such as home shopping, educational 
modules, and government information services for clients in the 
telecommunications, corporate, and broadcasting markets, will be 
developed using tools developed jointly by Digital and Digital 
Renaissance.  Digital Renaissance will also port its object database 
media management tools to the Digital server platform to complement 
and enhance existing software development tools developed by 
Digital.

     "Content development drives consumer demand for interactive 
services," said Sultan Zia, vice president of Digital's Video and 
Interactive Information Services group.  "That is why we are pleased 
to be working with Digital Renaissance, a leader in the creation of 
multimedia applications.  By making it significantly easier for 
content providers to develop a range of interactive programming, our 
relationship will accelerate the delivery of interactive information 
and entertainment services."

     "The types of tools and applications resulting from this 
agreement with Digital will be key links in the effective delivery 
of interactive broadband services to the home," said Keith Kocho, 
president and chief executive officer of Digital Renaissance.  
"Working with Digital's media server environment gives us the 
perfect opportunity to bring our experience in networked multimedia 
delivery to products that will play a strategic role in the growth 
of interactive services."

     Digital's media server platform has been selected by more cable 
and telephone companies worldwide than any other media server.  The 
company's Video and Interactive Information Architecture provides a 
full-service solution for delivering interactive video applications 
over many types of networks.  Digital's platform features object-
oriented middleware that links the world's fastest server systems -- 
based on 64-bit Alpha processors -- with the company's StorageWorks 
disk arrays and digital tape library systems.  This architecture 
also provides network, subscriber, and billing management 
capabilities in an open framework that supports third-party and 
legacy applications.

     Digital Renaissance Inc. is a new media engineering company 
that develops and applies interactive technologies.  The company 
creates client-specific, platform-independent multimedia 
applications for leading organizations in both the public and 
private sector.  Digital Renaissance also develops and integrates a 
broad range of networked multimedia technologies for clients in the 
telecommunications, broadcasting and technology sectors.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry- 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
