              DIGITAL EXTENDS PRESENCE IN $15 BILLION*
                   ASIA PACIFIC PERIPHERALS MARKET


           Signs Five Distributors and Expands Agreements
                       with Existing Partners


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 28, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced it has signed five new distributors and extended 
agreements with two partners in the Asia Pacific market, 
substantially broadening its presence in the region.  These new 
agreements will provide distributors and their customers with 
broader purchasing options and greater access to Digital's latest 
products. 

     New partners include First Tech Pacific Distributors and 
Powerful Impact (Malaysia); VST Computers (HK) Limited (China); 
Onflo Computer Company Limited, and Toppan Moore Computer Systems 
Limited (Hong Kong).  Extended agreements have been signed with 
existing partners, Chartered Systems and Networks of Singapore and 
SIS International of Hong Kong.  Distributors will now resell 
Digital's DEClaser 3500, DECwriter 500i and DECwriter 110i printers; 
VT and Dorio terminals; the new VT LAN40 windowing network terminal; 
and the Multia MultiClient Desktop device.

     "By expanding the number of distribution partners in Asia 
Pacific, end-users will have increased accessibility to Digital's 
products," said Karl McLean, manager, Asia Pacific Sales, Components 
and Peripherals Business Unit.  
"Digital's increased presence will allow Asia Pacific distributors 
and their customers the advantage of a more comprehensive product 
selection for their computing needs."

     "With distribution currently in Australia, Hong Kong and Japan, 
the addition of these new partners in China, Singapore, Korea and 
Malaysia enables us to provide an even higher level of support to 
customers," said Robin Dayne, Asia Pacific marketing and 
merchandising manager, Components and Peripherals Business Unit.

     The new Asia Pacific agreements are a part of Digital's overall 
distribution strategy to provide Digital products to existing 
customers and leverage market opportunities through relationships 
with distributors rather than using a direct sales model.  Digital, 
throughout 1995, will continue to aggressively expand these 
distributor partnerships.

     "We are excited to have signed this strategic partnership with 
Digital," said William Chung, executive director, Toppan Moore 
Computer Systems Limited.  "Adding Digital's technically superior 
products to our product mix will enable us to provide customers with 
cost-effective, quality solutions that reflect Digital's history of 
proven technology and engineering expertise."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
