     DIGITAL AND EDS SIGN AGREEMENT FOR DEVELOPMENT AND SUPPORT
                    OF IBM INTERCONNECT PRODUCTS


           Companies will work together to meet customers 
      current and future requirements for IBM SNA Connectivity

             
MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 30, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Electronic Data Systems (EDS) today announced the signing of a 
long-term development and support agreement for IBM Interconnect 
software products. The agreement is designed to meet customers' 
current and future requirements for IBM Interconnect products, and 
underscores Digital's on-going commitment to offer leadership 
products for integrating Digital and IBM SNA environments. 

     Under the agreement, EDS will enhance and maintain Digital's 
suite of IBM Interconnect products, including SNA gateways, client 
access software and terminal emulators.  These products allow PCs, 
UNIX systems, and OpenVMS systems to connect to IBM environments 
through a family of Digital gateways and are used by major worldwide 
customers to integrate enterprise-wide systems and to optimize their 
network investments.  Product directions and strategies for IBM 
Interconnect products will continue to be driven by Digital, based 
on customers business requirements, and Digital will continue to 
sell and service customers the products. 

     "This agreement demonstrates Digital's intent to partner with 
leading vendors to offer customers the best solutions to their 
business problems," said William R. Demmer, vice president of 
Digital's Software Business Group.  "Digital values the expertise 
that EDS, as well as our other 3rd party providers will bring to our 
family of IBM Interconnect products.  We look forward to working 
with EDS to deliver to our customers the best possible products, and 
to ensure that their investments in equipment and training are 
protected." 

     To insure continued synergy between these products and other 
Digital engineered networking products, EDS development engineers 
will initially be located in Digital's Network engineering 
headquarters, based in Littleton, MA.  As part of the agreement, EDS 
has made offers of employment to the current IBM Interconnect 
products engineering team. 

     Digital has been a leading provider of IBM Interconnect 
products with close to 20 years experience.  As part of this 
agreement Digital will continue to sell and service all products 
that result from this relationship.   

     "This agreement reflects a 'win-win-win' situation.  Digital 
wins, Digital's customers win, and EDS wins," said Kevin Malloy, 
Director, EDS Advanced Technology and Products Group.  "It is a 
further step in a growing and successful relationship between EDS 
and Digital which is focused on ensuring high levels of satisfaction 
among our mutual customers."

     EDS has operations in more than 35 countries, employs more than 
75,000 people and is the leader in applying information technology 
to meet the needs of businesses and governments worldwide.  Stock 
reflecting EDS' performance is traded on the New York Stock Exchange 
under the symbol GME.  EDS reported revenues of $10.05 billion in 1994.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
