                 DIGITAL'S MAILWORKS AND MAILBUS 400
              NOW AVAILABLE FOR OPENVMS ALPHA PLATFORMS


          . . . offers smooth upgrade for VAX customers . . .


    . . . new features, lower prices for Microsoft Mail users . . .


MAYNARD, Mass. -- April 4, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced new versions of its MailWorks and MAILbus 400 
electrponic messaging software for the OpenVMS Alpha operating 
system. Also available are new capabilities for users of Microsoft 
Mail who are networked to MailWorks servers.

     The MailWorks client/server software ties together diverse PC 
LAN messaging clients on a wide range of platforms including 
Macintosh, Microsoft Windows, DOS, and video terminals. It offers 
the reliability and security of host-based systems with the 
flexibility and ease-of-use of PC LAN mail systems.

     "MailWorks for OpenVMS on Digital's 64-bit AlphaServer systems 
provides a high-performance, state-of-the-art client/server solution 
that scales easily to tens of thousands of users," said William 
Demmer, vice president of Digital's software business group. "Our 
performance testing shows up to a 300% increase in the number of 
users supported over the previous version."


     MailWorks for OpenVMS Version 1.3 software now includes 
built-in support for direct use of cc:Mail for Windows Version 2, 
which transforms the PC LAN file sharing technology into powerful 
client/server enterprise messaging. cc:Mail users now have access to 
additional services provided by MailWorks such as secure, server-
based storage and Digital's Distributed Directory Services. Use of 
the MailWorks server software is transparent to cc:Mail users.

     The MailWorks server is now easily customized to support any 
site's configuration because of its new support for remote access to 
distributed directories, message stores and message routing 
software. In addition, the new MailWorks product extends its network 
support to include TGV, Inc.'s TCP/IP MultiNet and Wollongong's 
Pathway products.

     Digital also announced the availability of its industry leading 
MAILbus 400 X.400 transport agent software, and MAILbus 400 
Application Programming Interface (API) on OpenVMS for Alpha 
platforms. MAILbus 400 conforms to the CCITT 1992 X.400 standards 
and the MAILbus 400 API is an implementation of the X/Open Common 
Application Environment specifications. "Customers who want to 
deploy open, standards-based messaging systems as a solution to the 
problem of integrating, scaling and managing multi-vendor E-mail 
environments will benefit from the reliability, improved ease of 
use, and the higher performance of OpenVMS Alpha solutions," said 
Demmer.

     To help MailWorks customers plan and implement a smooth 
transition to the new MAILbus 400 environment, Digital announced 
today plans to support direct connectivity to MAILbus 400 and DEC 
X.500 Directory Services in the next version of MailWorks for 
OpenVMS, targeted for the end of 1995. To ease transition, the 
MAILbus 400 Message Router Gateway provides a direct, high 
performance connection between VAX based Message Router environments, 
and the Alpha OpenVMS X.400 environment.

     Also announced today are enhancements and new pricing for the 
Microsoft Mail Driver for MailWorks. Microsoft Mail users who are 
networked to the MailWorks server can now request delivery 
confirmation receipts in addition to read receipts. A new password 
feature now enables many Microsoft Mail users to share a single PC 
with secure inboxes and message store areas. Further, Microsoft Mail 
users may now control the flow of new mail messages to the desktop 
PC's disk. The new price of the Microsoft Mail Driver for MailWorks 
license is now $20 in packages of 100, a reduction of more than 50 
percent. It is available for both MailWorks for UNIX and MailWorks 
for OpenVMS servers.

     MailWorks for OpenVMS Version 1.3 for Alpha and VAX systems is 
available now. Prices range from $90 for a 1-user concurrent license 
to $4,000 for an unlimited capacity license. MAILbus 400 for OpenVMS 
is available now; pricing is $10,000 for an unlimited user license. 
The MAILbus 400 Application Programming Interface on OpenVMS Alpha 
is available now; price is $5,000.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
