          DIGITAL LOWERS U.S. AND LATIN AMERICA PRICES ON
     BROAD RANGE OF PC SERVERS AND SELECTED NOTEBOOK COMPUTERS

     
MAYNARD, Mass. -- April 20, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced price reductions in its Digital Prioris family of PC 
servers and in its Digital HiNote notebooks in the United States and 
Latin America/Caribbean region.  The new prices are as much as 26 
percent lower for select Prioris servers, and up to 24 percent lower 
for HiNote models.  The changes are effective immediately.

     Among the 10 Prioris models included in the reduction are the 
mid-range Prioris XL servers and the high-performance, Pentium-based 
Prioris HX introduced last December.  Prioris XL Server 466, 560, 
566, 590, and 590DP (dual processor) drop in list price as much as 
$1,500 U.S depending on the configuration.  A Prioris XL Server 
590DP now lists for $6,249 U.S., a drop of $1,500; the Prioris XL 
Server 590 lists for $4,619 U.S., a reduction of $930.  For the most 
powerful Prioris servers, list price cuts exceed $2,000 U.S. for the 
Prioris HX 590, which now lists for $6,619 or $10,289 depending on 
the configuration. 						    

     "Digital PCs are now even more affordable and continue to offer 
high-quality, high performance at very competitive prices," 
explained Skip Gladfelter, vice president, Americas marketing, 
Personal Computer Business Unit. "The marketplace has responded very 
positively to our PC servers pushing us to 6th place worldwide according 
to the 1994 Dataquest ranking."  That was the first year the company 
sold x86-based servers. 

Digital HiNote Notebook Prices Lowered

     Five Digital HiNote models have also been reduced in price. 
They include monochrome and color i486-based notebook computers.  
The reductions range from $90 to $650 U.S.  
New pricing is as follows:
	       	      			    	    Old U.S. New U.S.  
               	      			    	      List     List

HiNote CS 433 - SX/33  4MB RAM  170MB HD  DSTN mono  $1,699   $1,469

HiNote CS 433 - SX/33  4MB RAM  240MB HD  DSTN color  2,299    1,999

HiNote CS 450 - DX2/50  4MB RAM  340MB HD  DSTN color 2,699    2,049

HiNote CT 450 - DX2/50  4MB RAM  240MB HD  Active Matrix TFT color
	       	      			    	      3,229    3,139

HiNote CT 475 - DX4/75  4MB RAM  340MB HD  Active Matrix TFT color
	       	      			    	      3,999    3,539 


     "These price reductions underscore our resolve to be priced 
among the notebook leaders," said Gladfelter.  "Beyond the very 
attractive price, HiNote features innovative design in a light 
weight, thin notebook without compromising functionality."

Prioris Servers Earn Honors

     In benchmark testing by AIM Technology, an independent 
organization, the Prioris XL Server 590 finished first in the file 
server ranking and second in shared system testing in the Best 
Price/Sustained Performance Under $50,000 category.  The Prioris XL 590 
was also runner up in the file server testing for Best Sustained 
Performance Under $50,000 in a heavy system load environment.  These 
results are in AIM Technology's Spring 1995 UNIX System Price/Performance 
Guide.

     In a review of the Prioris HX 590, the April 1995 issue of SCO 
World magazine reported that "...for serious business applications 
requiring computing power, a  cost-effective upgrade path, and 
fault-tolerant hardware and software, you can't go wrong with the 
(Prioris) HX 590."

     Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit offers notebooks, 
desktops/deskside systems, and servers through resellers, 
distributors, systems integrators, and direct from Digital.  Digital 
PC has doubled unit shipments each of the past three calendar years 
and was ranked by Dataquest as number 11 in units shipped worldwide 
in 1994.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
