       DIGITAL SHOWCASES LEADERSHIP TECHNOLOGY AND WINDOWS NT
                 SOLUTIONS AT WINDOWS WORLD/COMDEX


        Windows NT on AlphaServer systems, World's Fastest 
            Workstation, and Multia Desktop Highlighted


WINDOWS WORLD, ATLANTA, GA -- April 24, 1995 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation is showcasing a full range of leadership Windows NT 
solutions, systems and services at Windows World/COMDEX. 
Highlighting Digital's exhibit are two BYTE Award winners from Fall 
COMDEX '94 - Multia Multiclient Desktop and Clusters Technology for 
Windows NT - as well as the newly announced AlphaStation 250 4/266 
and 233MHz Multia Desktop.  Independent software vendors and 
partners are also joining Digital to demonstrate their specific 
solutions in Digital's booth #8626.

To illustrate its Windows NT leadership position, Digital is 
offering the following demonstrations:

     o 	The new AlphaStation 250 4/266 - the world's fastest 
        workstation - using software compression in a video 
        conferencing application which emphasizes the availability 
        of third party commodity options.

     o  Clusters Technology for Windows NT - a technology 
        demonstration of Windows NT clusters, which won the BYTE 
        award for most significant technology at Fall COMDEX.  
        Digital's Clusters for Windows NT will enhance the 
        availability, scalability, and management of data and key 
        services within a client/server LAN environment.

     o  Multia Multiclient Desktop - BYTE Award winner for best 
        system at Fall COMDEX, Multia Desktop is an evolutionary 
        combination of Digital's Alpha technology, Microsoft Windows 
        NT, an optimized x11.R6 server and best-in-class terminal 
        emulators, resulting in end user application access with no 
        performance trade-offs.  Multia Desktop is the only product 
        that enables end users to simultaneously access UNIX, 
        Windows, Windows NT, and legacy applications while giving IS 
        managers key remote configuration management capabilities.

     o  AlphaServer family - Digital's award-winning AlphaServer 
        2100 4/275 4 CPU SMP server, AlphaServer 2000 4/200 2 CPU 
        SMP server, AlphaServer 1000 4/200 1 CPU SMP server serving 
        MPEG compressed video over the network to Windows-based PC 
        clients.  These AlphaServer systems are running Windows NT 
        Server and Version 3.5 SQL Server, and are serving movie 
        clips interactively from RAID-based disks to six PC
        clients.  This coordination of live video across the PCs 
        demonstrates high performance, high bandwidth, client/server 
        computing, using industry-standard software.

     o  eXcursion - Digital's client/server software that simplifies
        integration of UNIX and Windows NT systems while preserving 
        existing investments.  eXcursion allows the seamless 
        integration of Windows and Windows NT with X-windows 
        applications on a single desktop.

     o 	LinkWorks - Digital's award-winning solution framework for
        integrating personal productivity, groupware, and business 
        applications for line-of-business success.  LinkWorks 
        software group-enables these applications by adding 
        information sharing, document management, workflow 
        automation, and security. LinkWorks supports multi-vendor 
        clients and servers.

     o  ObjectBroker - a leading implementation of the popular
        Common Object Request Architecture (COBRA), Digital's
        ObjectBroker enables applications to interact across
        platform boundaries, providing investment protection for 
        existing and future software applications.

     o 	POLYCENTER products and services - an integrated, open 
        approach to managing distributed systems and networks. 
        Exhibits at the Digital booth include:

     	-  POLYCENTER NetView, a comprehensive network management 
           solution for heterogeneous, open networks.  Soon to be
           available on Windows NT, POLYCENTER NetView delivers the 
           combined strengths of Digital and IBM, the network    
           management leaders.

        -  POLYCENTER AssetWORKS extends Microsoft's System Manager 
           (MSM) to multivendor UNIX and OpenVMS systems allowing 
           management of UNIX, PC, and OpenVMS software assets from 
           a single Windows NT server. 

     o  Best Buy's Concept III Answer Center -  a best-in-class 
        solution, jointly developed by Digital, Microsoft, and 
        consumer electronics retailer Best Buy.  Their Answer Center 
        is an informational kiosk that provides fun, information and 
        education, while making it easier for the consumer to make 
        informed decisions. 

     o  Windows NT ISVs - Cheyenne Software, Gupta, Microsoft Visual 
        C++, Parametric Technology, ParcPlace, Powersoft, Saros, and 
        Watermak will be demonstrating their latest applications for 
        Windows NT.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
